{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at midnight.</b> This passage ought to have been placed immediately after the passage 'and he did not send the children of Israel out of his land,' so that all the plagues would be in order. The reason the passage of the new month was inserted in between is to inform you how the firstborn of Israel were spared when the destroyer came upon Egypt." "<b>At midnight and HaShem struck every firstborn.</b> And in another place it says 'on the day that I struck every firstborn.' Rabbi Yochanan said: even though He struck them at midnight, their souls convulsed within them until morning, so that Israel would know by which plague their enemies died. <b>And HaShem struck every firstborn.</b> Rabbi Elazar ben Pedat says: everywhere it says 'and HaShem,' it means He and His court and His Sanhedrin — this teaches that the heavenly court sat and decreed that the firstborn of Egypt should be struck down." "<b>From the firstborn of Pharaoh.</b> Scripture comes to teach you about Pharaoh, that he too was a firstborn, as it says: 'but for this purpose I have sustained you, etc.'" "<b>Who sits on his throne.</b> Who is destined to sit on his throne — this includes even an animal, as in the example: 'and he took his firstborn son who would reign in his stead.' One may say: in the four elements of the world Egypt was struck — water, wind, fire, dust. In the first two, blood and frogs — water. In the second two, lice and wild beasts — in the dust, as it is written: 'let the earth bring forth a living soul.' In the third two, pestilence and boils — pestilence came through tainted air, that is, wind; boils — 'blowing the furnace of fire,' came. In the fourth two, hail and locusts — through wind. The hail came from a storm wind that brings it, and likewise the locusts — the wind brings them. And the fifth two, through the works of the heavens, which is fire — such as darkness, that the luminaries withheld their light from the land of Egypt, and the plague of the firstborn — an angel descended from heaven to kill them. It turns out they were struck by water and wind and fire and dust. And these ten plagues were carried out by HaShem, and Moses, and Aaron: the first three by Aaron, in a lowly manner — two in water and the third in the dust of the earth. And by Moses, three in the upper realms, just as his rank is higher than Aaron's rank — and they are hail, locusts, darkness, for Moses ruled over heaven and earth. And by HaShem: wild beasts, pestilence, the plague of the firstborn, and one through all three of them — the plague of boils."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {3 "The 'fourth two' (arba'ot) appears to be a manuscript spelling variant for 'fourth pair'; rendered as 'fourth two' per the text given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:30.242726697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}